atterns are rather variable (Buck et al. 2008) and the Greenland specimens tend to have reduced pale markings compared to North American specimens. A detailed description of the species is available in Buck et al. (2008). Ancistrocerus waldenii was seen to be abundant in the area around Kangerlussuaq, and specimens were repeatedly seen flying over low vegetation or on open paths and dirt roads where females were seen collecting clay for nest building. On Disko Island, several specimens were observed flying along an open path near a stream in a low mountain meadow (69 ° 15 ' 34 '' N, 53 ° 32 ' 34 '' W) (Fig. 2 a) close to Qeqertarsuaq. The vegetation in the area was composed mostly of glaucous willow (Salix glauca L.) and dwarf shrubs, with mosses, sedges, and lush stands of dwarf fireweed (Chamerion latifolium (L.) Holub) along the stream flowing through the area.","","text","",""]]},"KTXC":{"d":[["","NL","iso","",""],["","SE","iso","",""],["","TR","iso","",""],["Ul'yanovsk","","text","",""]]},"KVKV8":{"d":[["China (Sichuan, Zhejiang); China (Taiwan), Taiwan.","","text","",""],["Eastpalaearctic","","text","",""],["Oriental","","text","",""]]},"L2PTX":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"L2Q3X":{"d":[["Ethiopia","","text","native",""]]},"L7PG":{"d":[["China (Guangxi)","","text","",""]]},"LC92":{"d":[["","CLM-OO","tdwg","native",""],["Colombia","","text","native",""]]},"LC9PB":{"d":[["Singaporean Exclusive Economic Zone","8485","mrgid","native",""]]},"LFR6":{"d":[["Guatemala","","text","native",""]]},"LG23B":{"d":[["","PAK","tdwg","",""]]},"LHPRD":{"d":[["","CO","iso","native",""]]},"LKSCM":{"d":[["Distribution. Madagascar, South Africa.","","text","",""]]},"LV2F":{"d":[["Nile delta","3867","mrgid","",""]]},"LYKJ":{"d":[["Neotropical(Mexico:Durango, Hidalgo, México, Michoacán, Morelos, Oaxaca)","","text","",""]]},"M4SF":{"d":[["","ORE-OO","tdwg","native",""],["","WAS-OO","tdwg","native",""],["USA (OR,WA)","","text","native",""]]},"M6G88":{"d":[["Southern Asia","